# Licensing

This repository holds three kinds of material, and they are not under the same
terms. Read the section that covers what you want to use.

## The data — CC BY 4.0

**Everything under `data-exports/`, and the parameter register in
`site-src/data/history.yaml`, is released under the Creative Commons
Attribution 4.0 International licence (CC BY 4.0).**

https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

You may share and adapt it, including commercially, provided you give
appropriate credit. That is what it is published for: the register exists so it
can be downloaded, checked and cited.

Attribution should name the Bari group and this site, and — when you use the
numbers of a particular release — cite the paper that release came from. Every
record in the register carries its own `arxiv`, `journal` and `table` fields
naming its source; those are the papers to cite. The 2025 release is:

> F. Capozzi, W. Giarè, E. Lisi, A. Marrone, A. Melchiorri, A. Palazzo,
> *Neutrino masses and mixing: Entering the era of subpercent precision*,
> Phys. Rev. D **111**, 093006 (2025), doi:10.1103/PhysRevD.111.093006

A citation to this site is not a substitute for citing the paper a number came
from.

## The code and the prose — all rights reserved

The build system, the generators and the tests (`build.py`, `tools/`), and the
written content of the pages (`site-src/content/`, and the rendered pages under
`site/`), are **© the authors, all rights reserved**.

They are public so the site can be built, inspected and audited — the point of
publishing the generators is that anyone can see how a number reaches a page —
but no licence to reuse or redistribute them is granted here. If you want to
reuse any of it, ask.

## Third-party material — its own terms, as credited on the page

Some material on this site belongs to other people and travels under its own
licence, which this file does not and cannot override:

- **Figures from published papers** are reproduced under the licence of the
  paper they come from. The figures from Phys. Rev. D 111, 093006 (2025) are
  used under CC BY 4.0, with the authors, title, journal and DOI credited
  beside each one, as that licence requires.
- **Photographs** come from Wikimedia Commons under CC BY 4.0, CC BY-SA 4.0 or
  in the public domain. Each carries its author, its licence and a link to its
  file page on Commons, in the card that shows it. A CC BY-SA photograph
  remains CC BY-SA: reusing it obliges you to the same terms.
- **Coastline geometry** in the world map derives from Natural Earth, which is
  in the public domain.

Where a page credits a source, that credit is the licence statement for that
item. Removing it is not permitted for any of the above.
